                    <div class="divider"></div>
                </div>

                <!-- Category: Network & Connectivity -->
                <div class="faq-category">
                    <h3>Network & Connectivity</h3>
                    
                    <details class="faq-item">
                        <summary>Why is my Wi-Fi not working?</summary>
                        <div class="faq-content">
                            <p><strong>Steps:</strong> Ensure Wi-Fi is enabled on your device. Restart your device. Check if other devices can connect to the same network. If on a laptop, look for a physical Wi-Fi switch.</p>
                            <p><strong>Stop & Report:</strong> Stop troubleshooting and log a ticket if the network name (SSID) is missing, or if multiple users are experiencing the same issue.</p>
                        </div>
                    </details>
                    
                    <details class="faq-item">
                        <summary>Why can't I connect to the internet?</summary>
                        <div class="faq-content">
                            <p><strong>Steps:</strong> Check your ethernet cable connections if hardwired. Verify your router/modem is powered on. Restart your browser and clear the cache.</p>
                            <p><strong>Stop & Report:</strong> Stop if you receive specific proxy or DNS error messages, and report the issue to IT support.</p>
                        </div>
                    </details>
                </div>

                <!-- Category: Devices & Hardware -->
                <div class="faq-category">
                    <h3>Devices & Hardware</h3>
                    
                    <details class="faq-item">
                        <summary>What should I do if my computer is running slowly?</summary>
                        <div class="faq-content">
                            <p><strong>Steps:</strong> Close unused applications and browser tabs. Perform a system restart. Check your hard drive for available space.</p>
                            <p><strong>Stop & Report:</strong> Log a ticket if the computer crashes, makes unusual hardware noises, or remains slow after a reboot.</p>
                        </div>
                    </details>

                    <details class="faq-item">
                        <summary>What should I do if my printer is not responding?</summary>
                        <div class="faq-content">
                            <p><strong>Steps:</strong> Verify the printer is turned on and has paper/toner. Clear any visible paper jams. Cancel stuck documents in the print queue and restart the printer.</p>
                            <p><strong>Stop & Report:</strong> Report the issue if the printer displays an internal hardware error code or if it disappears completely from your network devices list.</p>
                        </div>
                    </details>
                </div>

                <!-- Category: Accounts & Access -->
                <div class="faq-category">
                    <h3>Accounts & Access</h3>
                    
                    <details class="faq-item">
                        <summary>What should I do if my password is not working?</summary>
                        <div class="faq-content">
                            <p><strong>Steps:</strong> Ensure Caps Lock is off. Carefully retype your password. Try logging into a different company portal to verify if the account is locked.</p>
                            <p><strong>Stop & Report:</strong> If you receive a "Account Locked" message or have forgotten the password entirely, submit a ticket for a secure password reset.</p>
                        </div>
                    </details>

                    <details class="faq-item">
                        <summary>Why can't I access a shared network folder?</summary>
                        <div class="faq-content">
                            <p><strong>Steps:</strong> Check your internet/VPN connection. Restart your file explorer. Verify the folder path is correct.</p>
                            <p><strong>Stop & Report:</strong> Log a ticket if you get an "Access Denied" error, as your user permissions may need to be modified.</p>
                        </div>
                    </details>
                </div>

                <!-- Category: Ticket Management -->
                <div class="faq-category">
                    <h3>Ticket Management</h3>
                    
                    <details class="faq-item">
                        <summary>How do I report a recurring technical problem?</summary>
                        <div class="faq-content">
                            <p><strong>Steps:</strong> Download the IT Ticket Management Workbook. Clearly state that this is a recurring issue and reference any previous ticket numbers if available.</p>
                            <p><strong>Stop & Report:</strong> Do not attempt advanced registry or system changes. Let technical support investigate the root cause.</p>
                        </div>
                    </details>

                    <details class="faq-item">
                        <summary>What information should I include in an IT support ticket?</summary>
                        <div class="faq-content">
                            <p><strong>Steps:</strong> Include your name, date/time, affected device, a clear description of the issue, specific error messages, impact on your work, and what you have already tried to fix it.</p>
                        </div>
                    </details>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Escalation Policy Section -->
            <div class="escalation-section mt-4 bg-light card">
                <div class="section-title">
                    <h2>Escalation Policy</h2>
                    <div class="divider"></div>
                </div>
                <p class="mb-2">Critical incidents should be prioritized and escalated promptly. Tickets should be escalated when the issue exceeds the current support level's capabilities, remains unresolved beyond the applicable target time, or poses a significant business or security risk.</p>
                
                <div class="escalation-levels">
                    <div class="level-card">
                        <h4>Level 1 — First-Line Support</h4>
                        <p>Basic troubleshooting, password assistance, connectivity checks, and initial ticket logging.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="level-card">
                        <h4>Level 2 — Technical Support</h4>
                        <p>More complex device, network, software, and recurring technical issues.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="level-card">
                        <h4>Level 3 — Specialist/Senior IT</h4>
                        <p>Critical incidents, complex infrastructure problems, and issues requiring specialist investigation.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="escalation-flow mt-3">
                    <h3>Escalation Flow</h3>
                    <div class="flow-diagram">
                        <div class="flow-box">User Logs Ticket</div>
                        <div class="flow-arrow">➔</div>
                        <div class="flow-box">Level 1 Investigates</div>
                        <div class="flow-arrow">➔</div>
                        <div class="flow-box">Escalation (if unresolved)</div>
                        <div class="flow-arrow">➔</div>
                        <div class="flow-box">Level 2 / 3 Resolves</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Change Request Form -->
